{"seq":13,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T03:02:56.179Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"6f949341e3d4e20bf924e6fc73463da1ab6d64bc71e9e1729e3ad66b4911fef5","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"@bettina.kroll Here's the list from the Coastal channels and Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet. Pellow Home Living is excluded.\n\nPellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)\n- Ticket #4419: Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length. Open per Moss's cheat sheet. The 2025-11-02 digest attaches #4419 to Puget Sound (see the conflict below).\n- Gate 4 chassis pool validation during shift change: the main friction point. No ticket number in these sources.\n\nDriftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)\n- Ticket #4419: barge slip 7 schedule sync, logged by Kwame's port account per Moss's 2025-11-02 digest. Same number as the PHL ticket above, so one of the two entries is probably wrong.\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by warehouse managers.\n- Tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch. No ticket number cited.\n- Patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift (2025-11-02 digest). It may be the same request as the manual CSV patch above; the sources don't say.\n\nLeft out: Pellow Home Living items (PD-4821, ticket #8812, the Covey report label), and Saltmarsh items (PD-4824, PD-4827). Your own cutover recap also mentions PHL ticket PD-8841 (Gate 4B chassis holds). I left it out because it's outside the sources you named. Tell me if you want it added.\n\nPlease confirm which account #4419 belongs to before Kwame's review."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
